Resonance Parameter Information                                   2237 1451
-------------------------------                                   2237 1451
                                                                  2237 1451
 COVARIANCE FILE: resonance parameters (MF 32)                    2237 1451
 Author:  L. Leal, July, 2009  (ORNL)                             2237 1451
                                                                  2237 1451
 Resolved resonance covariance data were generate with the SAMMY  2237 1451
 [ref1] code for Ti isotopes.  SAMMY was run with the option of   2237 1451
 generating resonance-covariance retroactively using the          2237 1451
 "propagated uncertainty parameter" option to include systematic  2237 1451
 data uncertainties.[ref2, ref3].                                 2237 1451
    [ref 1] N. M. Larson, "Updated Users' Guide for SAMMY," Oak   2237 1451
             Ridge National Laboratory report  ORNL/TM-9179/R6    2237 1451
             (2003)                                               2237 1451
    [ref 2] L. C. Leal, N. M. Larson, H. Derrien, T. Kawano, and  2237 1451
            M. B Chadwick, "A New Approach fo Nuclear Data        2237 1451
            Covariances and Sensitivity Generation," International2237 1451
            Conference on Nuclear Data for Science and Technology,2237 1451
            " Santa Fe, New Mexico, September 26 - October 1,     2237 1451
            2004.                                                 2237 1451
    [ref 3] L. C. Leal, G. Arbanas, H. Derrien, N. M. Larson, and 2237 1451
            B. Rearden, "Covariance data for U-233 in the Resolved2237 1451
            Resonance Region for Criticality Safey Applicatioins,"2237 1451
            Mathematics and Computation, Supercomputing, Reactor  2237 1451
            Physics and Nuclear and Biological Applications,      2237 1451
            Palais des Papes, Avignon, France, September 12-15,   2237 1451
            2005.                                                 2237 1451
