mf=2  Resonance parameters                                        2237 1451
 mt=151  Resolved resonance parameters                            2237 1451
   Resolved parameters for MLBW formula were given in the energy  2237 1451
   region from 1.0e-5 eV to 300 keV.  Parameters were taken from  2237 1451
   ref./5/, for positive resonances.  Parameters for negative     2237 1451
   resonance were obtained so that the reproduced cross sections  2237 1451
   for both scattering and capture gave the 2200 m/s value of     2237 1451
   3.7+-0.3 and 0.179+-0.003 barns, respectively/5/.  The         2237 1451
   scattering radius was assumed to be 4.5 fermi.  Calculated 22002237 1451
   m/sec cross sections and resonance integrals are as follows:   2237 1451
                                                                  2237 1451
            2200 m/s cross section(b)     res. integral(b)        2237 1451
    elastic        3.74                                           2237 1451
    capture        0.18                     0.088                 2237 1451
    total          3.92                                           2237 1451
                                                                  2237 1451
mf=3  Neutron cross sections                                      2237 1451
  Below 300 keV, no background cross section was given.           2237 1451
                                                                  2237 1451
  The calculation with sincros-ii system/2/ was made by adopting  2237 1451
  Walter-Guss omp modified by Yamamuro/2/ for neutron, Perey omp  2237 1451
  /6/ for proton, Lemos omp modified by Arthur and Young/7/       2237 1451
  for alpha, Lohr-Haeberli omp/8/ for deuteron, Becchettii-       2237 1451
  Greenlees omp/9/ for triton and He-3, and standard level        2237 1451
  density parameters of sincros-ii system.                        2237 1451
                                                                  2237 1451
 mt=1 Total                                                       2237 1451
   Below 300 keV, created from the resonance parameters.          2237 1451
   Above 300 keV, optical and statistical model calculation was   2237 1451
   made with the casthy code/10/.                                 2237 1451
   The optical potential parameters used are:                     2237 1451
         V = 50.75 - 0.120*En,    Vso = 4.72   (MeV)              2237 1451
        Ws = 10.9 - 0.234*En,      Wv = 0.0    (MeV)              2237 1451
         r = 1.26,   rs = 1.02,   rso = 1.16    (fm)              2237 1451
         a = 0.52,  aso = 0.52,     b = 0.40    (fm)              2237 1451
                                                                  2237 1451
 mt=2 Elastic scattering                                          2237 1451
   Obtained by subtracting the sum of the partial cross sections  2237 1451
   from the total cross section.                                  2237 1451
